  <revision rev="2" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>ce17b0514e5c749541907fb982afea9b</srcmd5>
    <version>3.5.1</version>
    <time>1795619578</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>- Update to 3.5.1
  * No code changes, patch bump only to address a git tag snafu
- Updates from 3.4.0 -&gt; 3.5.0
  * Highlights:
    - Support for TOML v1.1.0
    - Support for C++20 std::chrono types
    - C++20 module support with import tomlplusplus;
    - Faster parsing and formatting
    - Faster compiles and smaller binaries
    - Floats print in their shortest round-trip form with every compiler
    - Many fixes for crashes and undefined behaviour
    - Meson users: a default Meson build is now header-only. This is a bugfix
      for a regression that was accidentally introduced in v3.4.0 where the
      default became a shared library build, despite the documentation stating
      otherwise. If you want to keep shared library builds, you must specify
      -Dbuild_lib=true.
  * Bugs fixed:
    - Fixed assertion failure when parsing some incomplete date-times
      (gh#marzer/tomlplusplus#313)
    - Fixed is_homogeneous() overloads with first_nonmatch outparam being
      broken in optimized builds (gh#marzer/tomlplusplus#231)
    - Fixed unclear error message when parsing integers that would overflow
      (gh#marzer/tomlplusplus#224)
    - Fixed CMake install target installing meson.build files
      (gh#marzer/tomlplusplus#236)
    - Fixed &quot;unresolved symbol&quot; error with nvc++ (gh#marzer/tomlplusplus#220)
    - Fixed stack overflow when parsing deeply nested dotted keys
      (gh#marzer/tomlplusplus#242)
    - Fixed assertion failure when parsing some malformed documents
      (gh#marzer/tomlplusplus#321)</comment>
    <requestid>1400418</requestid>
  </revision>
</revisionlist>
